<task id="010" project="spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Author staticwebapp.config.json + SWA deploy workflow</title>
    <phase>1 Hosting migration + routing</phase>
    <gate>blocked</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Deploy config + CI workflow (ci-workflows hot path)</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Config authoring following SWA conventions</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe reason="shares .github/workflows + config with 003/014">false</parallel-safe>
    <deps>003</deps>
    <tags>azure, deploy, ci-cd</tags>
    <estimated-effort>0.5-1 dev-day</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Author `src/client/external-spa/staticwebapp.config.json` with a `navigationFallback` rewrite to `/index.html` (excluding static asset paths) plus `Referrer-Policy: no-referrer-or-same-origin` and an explicit CSP `frame-ancestors`, AND a GitHub Actions SWA deploy workflow under `.github/workflows/` that builds and deploys the external-spa, superseding (but not deleting) the Power Pages `scripts/Deploy-ExternalWorkspaceSpa.ps1` path. Use `npm install --legacy-peer-deps` (not `npm ci`) and the production build script; read the build command and output dir from the repo rather than assuming them.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    You are a DevOps + frontend-hosting engineer configuring Azure Static Web Apps (SWA)
    hosting for the Spaarke external-spa. You author deploy configuration and CI workflow
    following SWA conventions; you do not redesign the SPA.
  </role>

  <goal>
    Produce a `staticwebapp.config.json` for `src/client/external-spa/` that (a) rewrites all
    unknown paths to `/index.html` via `navigationFallback` so BrowserRouter deep links resolve,
    and (b) sends security headers (`Referrer-Policy: no-referrer-or-same-origin` and an explicit
    CSP `frame-ancestors`); AND a GitHub Actions SWA deploy workflow under `.github/workflows/`
    that builds and deploys the external-spa, superseding `scripts/Deploy-ExternalWorkspaceSpa.ps1`
    (the Power Pages web-resource deploy path).
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      The external-spa currently ships to Power Pages as a web resource via
      `scripts/Deploy-ExternalWorkspaceSpa.ps1` and uses HashRouter (task 011 flips it to
      BrowserRouter). BrowserRouter deep links (e.g. `/project/{id}`) only resolve if the host
      rewrites unknown paths to the SPA entry — on SWA that is `navigationFallback`. Phase 1
      runs on the EXISTING Entra B2B identity so any routing regression is attributable to
      routing, not the IdP. This task authors ONLY the SWA config + workflow; the routing code
      change is task 011 and the actual deploy/parity verification is task 014.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file status="new">src/client/external-spa/staticwebapp.config.json</file>
      <file status="new">.github/workflows/ (new SWA deploy workflow, e.g. deploy-external-spa-swa.yml)</file>
      <file status="reference">scripts/Deploy-ExternalWorkspaceSpa.ps1 (the Power Pages path this supersedes)</file>
      <file status="reference">src/client/external-spa/package.json (build script for the workflow)</file>
      <file status="reference">src/client/external-spa/vite.config.ts (build output dir)</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">
      SCOPE: the SWA config and workflow. BrowserRouter requires a `navigationFallback`
      rewrite to `/index.html` (excluding static asset paths) AND the app must render an
      in-app 404 for unknown routes (the in-app 404 itself is task 011). MUST provide the
      navigationFallback rewrite here so 011's routing has a working host.
    </constraint>
    <constraint source="spec-FR-04">
      SCOPE: the response headers block. MUST emit `Referrer-Policy` (`no-referrer-or-same-origin`)
      and an explicit CSP `frame-ancestors`. MUST NOT emit an `X-Frame-Options` that conflicts
      with the CSP `frame-ancestors` directive.
    </constraint>
    <constraint source="spec-scope">
      SCOPE: deploy path only. The workflow supersedes `scripts/Deploy-ExternalWorkspaceSpa.ps1`
      but does NOT delete it — decommission of the Power Pages path is Phase 3 (task not in this batch).
    </constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md-node">
      SCOPE: the workflow's install step. Use `npm install --legacy-peer-deps --no-audit --no-fund`,
      NOT `npm ci`, and build with the production build script (not a bare `npm run build` if a
      prod script exists).
    </constraint>
  </constraints>

  <justification>
    <existing>Deploy-ExternalWorkspaceSpa.ps1 (Power Pages web-resource deploy path) is the only existing deploy mechanism for the external-spa.</existing>
    <extension>No — the SWA hosting model differs fundamentally from the Power Pages web-resource model (static-host rewrites + header config vs. Dataverse web resource upload); the PowerShell script cannot be extended into a SWA deploy.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Without `staticwebapp.config.json`, BrowserRouter deep links 404 on direct navigation (no navigationFallback rewrite) and the SWA sends no Referrer-Policy / CSP frame-ancestors headers, leaving FR-02 and FR-04 unmet and Teams-readiness framing unowned.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>docs/guides/EXTERNAL-ACCESS-SPA-GUIDE.md</file>
      <file>.claude/skills/azure-deploy/SKILL.md</file>
      <file>src/client/external-spa/package.json</file>
      <file>src/client/external-spa/vite.config.ts</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="prescriptive">
    <step>Read `src/client/external-spa/package.json` and `vite.config.ts` to determine the build command and the build output directory (SWA `app_location` / `output_location`).</step>
    <step>Author `src/client/external-spa/staticwebapp.config.json` with a `navigationFallback` block rewriting unknown paths to `/index.html`, excluding static asset globs (e.g. `/assets/*`, `*.{js,css,ico,png,svg,woff2}`).</step>
    <step>Add a `globalHeaders` (or route-level headers) block emitting `Referrer-Policy: no-referrer-or-same-origin` and a `Content-Security-Policy` with an explicit `frame-ancestors` directive. Do not add a conflicting `X-Frame-Options`.</step>
    <step>Add a `responseOverrides` 404 mapping only if needed to route to the SPA entry; otherwise rely on navigationFallback + the in-app 404 (task 011).</step>
    <step>Author the `.github/workflows/` SWA deploy workflow (Azure/static-web-apps-deploy action) that installs deps with `npm install --legacy-peer-deps --no-audit --no-fund`, builds the external-spa, and deploys the build output to the SWA. Use the SWA deployment token from a repository secret; do not hardcode secrets.</step>
    <step>Verify the JSON is valid and the workflow YAML parses; cross-check `app_location`/`output_location` against the actual Vite output dir.</step>
  </steps>

  <outputs>
    <output>src/client/external-spa/staticwebapp.config.json with navigationFallback + security headers</output>
    <output>.github/workflows/ SWA deploy workflow that builds + deploys the external-spa</output>
    <output>Task notes recording the build command, output dir, and the secret name used for the SWA token</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">`navigationFallback` in staticwebapp.config.json rewrites an unknown path (e.g. `/project/abc`) to `/index.html`, while static asset paths are excluded from the rewrite.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Response headers config emits `Referrer-Policy: no-referrer-or-same-origin` AND a Content-Security-Policy containing an explicit `frame-ancestors` directive.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No `X-Frame-Options` header is emitted that conflicts with the CSP `frame-ancestors` directive (negative case).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The workflow builds the external-spa and deploys it to SWA; it uses `npm install --legacy-peer-deps` (NOT `npm ci`) and references the SWA token from a secret (no hardcoded secret — negative case).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`scripts/Deploy-ExternalWorkspaceSpa.ps1` is NOT deleted by this task (decommission is Phase 3 — negative case).</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    Phase 1 deliberately stays on Entra B2B. The output dir and build command MUST be read from
    the repo, not assumed. The in-app 404 route lives in task 011; this task only guarantees the
    host rewrites so that route can render.
  </notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
  </execution>
</task>
